Subject: [PATCH] 3106 (speed): the server finds the weather, and the first
 turn answers

The tester's 58029: the weather line answered in 18.0 / 19.2 / 19.1 s
against a 12 s target. Thread 51349's timeline: 6 s before the forced
web search began (a whole model turn spent deciding to call it), 2.8 s
of search, 7.6 s for the answer turn.

A weather run now has the server run that one web search itself
(costed, logged as web_search:weather, its results registered like the
model's own) and hand the results over in the opening-search section, the
same text a goal's opening search uses. The model answers in its first
turn. If the server's search fails or comes back empty, the run falls
back to the forced search as before. No new model-facing text.

